e to ask  please do so now  just click on the ask a question box  located on the far left of your screen  all right your first question is  as an antimicrobial stewardship  pharmacist  how can i motivate physicians to  actually integrate  pro calcite and ordering and  interpretation  to their practice at my hospital yeah  good good question  so how do you get people to use it  because this is really the tool of the  hospitalist  less than the id doctor because the  patients we see are very complicated  and difficult sometimes to interpret and  so i think the way to do this is to  build this into standardized protocols  whether that's you build it into your  community acquired pneumonia  whether you build that into your  exacerbations of copd order set  your sepsis order sets and then i think  it helps to  have a champion for that and then  utilize that to utilize that person or  those persons  to uh to move this forward so for our  facility we use our pharmacist a lot  and so we developed basically some  guidance on exacerbations of copd  we did a bunch of education for our  clinicians we put this  you know pro customer order set  developed an order set and then  um our team based pharmacists actually  look at procalcitonin and say hey the  pro costs are really low  can we stop the antibiotics and so i  think one thing you have to do is  educate people but you also have to sort  of remind them because  education doesn't always doesn't stick  and so it helps to build it in  that this is how we manage things and  these are our guidance so you have to  make people aware  build it into their practice and then  remind them that that's their practice  eventually they kind of learn that  that's how we do things  great thank you okay your next question  is there any data that supports the role  of pct biomarker use  in changing antimicrobial agent and or  dose  yeah i don't know for dose uh you know  where you would use it to change  antimicrobial agent would be perhaps  th